      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before African American residents moved in, Old Oakland’s hills were known as the “Bible Belt” because of the white Protestant community that lived there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Oakland%2C_Oakland%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During World War II, Old Oakland experienced a home‑building boom on land previously zoned for industry to house workers needed for war industries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Oakland%2C_Oakland%2C_California",
